name issue_335_fps1_keyframe_packets
describe 1 fps video next to audio on a clean 2 Mbps link: no keyframe request while a long keyframe arrives, so audio stays near libwebrtc's delay (issue #335)
duration 30s
seed 1
video_fps 1
# compare_seeds 80 (#770): video.pause_total_ms is decided by whether one seed's longest gap
# between rendered frames crosses the 5 s pause threshold. At 1 fps one frame more or less
# moves it: seed 4 renders 17 frames on main c77c654 (one 5.8 s pause) against 18 before #716
# (no pause), and ours pauses on 20 of seeds 1-80 (16 before #577).
compare_seeds 80
at 0s capacity=2Mbps delay=40ms
# The Tester's repro (#335). The first keyframe takes ~0.5 s to arrive; the
# receiver counted only its first packet as a keyframe packet, asked for
# another keyframe at 400 ms, and the 4x keyframes then filled the bottleneck.
# libwebrtc M157 on this scenario (sm_compare, yardstick PR #338, seeds 1-10):
# mouth-to-ear p95 823-1040 ms (mean 890), jitter buffer p95 680-780 ms,
# concealed 0.03-1.1 %, queue p95 63-302 ms, no keyframe requests, render fps
# 0.93-1.0. Bounds sit just above ours on seeds 1-5 and not above libwebrtc's
# worst seed.
# Target (issue #335, Tester): mouth-to-ear p95 < 400, jb p95 < 300; libwebrtc
# doesn't meet those either at 1 fps.
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on): was == 0. Provisional lock, tracked to #375 (Owner option A, 2026-10-24): ours 2 on seed 1, libwebrtc worst seed 1-10 1 (mean 0.1).
# Issue #375 (Opus size model calibrated to libopus): ours 1 on seed 1 (0.6 over seeds 1-10), libwebrtc's worst seed 1. Tight.
# Issue #375 (the encoder activity check and allocation probe, as VideoSendStreamImpl): ours 0 on seed 1 (0 over seeds 1-10), libwebrtc mean 0.1. Back to == 0.
expect video.keyframe_requests == 0
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on): was >= 0.99. Provisional lock, tracked to #375: ours 0.333 on seed 1, libwebrtc worst seed 1-10 0.567 (mean 0.827).
# Issue #375 (Opus size model): ours 0.367 on seed 1 (mean 0.59 over seeds 1-10), still below libwebrtc's worst seed: provisional, #375.
# Issue #375 (encoder activity check): ours 0.833 on seed 1 (mean 0.80 over seeds 1-10; libwebrtc 0.767 on seed 1, mean 0.827). Tight.
# Issue #375 (the activity check runs before a reconfiguration at the same instant; program.md 0.2): was >= 0.8.
# Ours 0.767 on seed 1, as libwebrtc's seed 1 (0.767; worst of 1-10 0.567, mean 0.827); our mean 0.81 over seeds 1-10.
# Owner sign-off on #388: 10 % below ours, above libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect video.render_fps >= 0.69
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on; program.md 0.2, needs-human): were < 910, < 750 and < 0.7. Ours on
# seed 1: 1893, 1060 and 3.76; libwebrtc's worst of seeds 1-10 on this PR's compare-webrtc at f910c0a: 2187, 1440
# and 4.92 (means 979, 806, 0.52). Owner's rule: 10-30 % margin, never beyond libwebrtc's worst seed.
# Issue #375 (Opus size model): ours 1596, 1020 and 3.42 on seed 1 (mean m2e 1399 over seeds 1-10); 10 % above ours.
# Issue #375 (encoder activity check): ours 914, 730 and 0.62 on seed 1 (mean m2e 914 over seeds 1-10; libwebrtc 802, 720 and 0
# on seed 1, means 979, 806, 0.52); 10 % above ours.
# Issue #375 (activity check before a reconfiguration): mouth-to-ear was < 1010. Ours 831, 730 and 0 on seed 1 (mean m2e 892
# over seeds 1-10; libwebrtc 802, 720 and 0 on seed 1); 10 % above ours for mouth-to-ear, the other two unchanged.
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 915
expect audio.jb_delay_p95_ms < 810
expect audio.concealed_pct < 0.7
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on): was < 195. Provisional lock, tracked to #375: ours 800 on seed 1, libwebrtc worst seed 1-10 699 (mean 127).
# Issue #375 (Opus size model): ours 541 on seed 1 (mean 410 over seeds 1-10), within libwebrtc's worst seed. Tight.
# Issue #375 (encoder activity check): ours 150 on seed 1 (mean 140 over seeds 1-10; libwebrtc 37 on seed 1, mean 127); 10 % above ours.
# Issue #375 (activity check before a reconfiguration): was < 165. Ours 64.6 on seed 1 (mean 122 over seeds 1-10; libwebrtc 37 on
# seed 1, mean 127); 10 % above ours.
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 72
